                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00/30393: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Vice Consul at Ciudad Juarez</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Scherer</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ciudad
                                Juarez</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-08-11T20:00:00-06:00">August 11, 1936—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 12—12:49 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Referring to the Embassy’s telegram August 11, noon. Nicolas Rodriquez landed at
                    Ciudad Juarez 5 p.m., was accompanied by General Juan Felipe Rico, garrison
                    commander, to International Bridge, was admitted by American immigration
                    authorities 6 o’clock. Probably will spend night in El Paso. No demonstrations.
                    Embassy informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Scherer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
